From c555d3960e11b07054d9c017d69473df0b89a78f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Z (assistant)" <z-ai-assistant@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(frontend): wire up missing routes, complete SchedulePage,
 add action CTAs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The frontend had three blocking issues that left it without any buttons to
generate or schedule anything:

1. SchedulePage.tsx was unfinished — the file ended with a
   `// __SCHEDULE_JSX__` placeholder where the return statement should
   have been, so it would not even compile if it were rendered.

2. App.tsx only wired four routes — /, /auth, /auth/callback, /dashboard —
   so every other nav link (Projects, Schedule, Connect, Billing, Profile,
   Admin) silently fell through to the landing page. ProjectsPage.tsx and
   SchedulePage.tsx were already fully built but were dead code.

3. The Bun dev server (src/index.ts) only proxied /api/projects as an exact
   path, so calls like /api/projects/{id}/generate, /api/jobs/{id},
   /api/videos/{id}/media, /api/schedules, /api/social/accounts,
   /api/pipeline/status, /api/oauth/{platform}/authorize all returned 404
   from the dev server — even the existing code couldn't have worked.

Fixes:

* Complete SchedulePage.tsx with the missing return JSX: a scheduling form
  (video picker, platform picker, datetime-local picker), an upcoming-posts
  list with cancel buttons, and a published-posts list with live links.

* Rewrite App.tsx with a tiny URL→component router covering every page in
  the build prompt's FRONTEND PAGES section: /dashboard, /projects,
  /schedule, /connect, /billing, /profile, /onboarding, /admin.

* Update src/index.ts to serve index.html for every new page route, and add
  the missing API proxy wildcards: /api/pipeline/status, /api/projects/*,
  /api/videos/*, /api/jobs/*, /api/schedules/*, /api/published-posts,
  /api/social/accounts/*, /api/oauth/*.

* Rewrite DashboardPage.tsx with the prominent action CTAs the user was
  looking for: Create a project (→ /projects), Schedule a post (→ /schedule),
  Connect a platform (→ /connect), Upgrade your plan (→ /billing), and an
  admin-only Open admin panel button. Adds a status row (plan, connected
  platforms, account role) and a 3-step 'How it works' card.

* Create the five missing page components referenced by the new routing:
  ConnectPage (OAuth flow + disconnect, surfaces platform limitations
  honestly), BillingPage (Stripe checkout + portal), ProfilePage (name,
  email, password change), AdminPage (metrics dashboard + audit log, with
  non-admin guard card), OnboardingPage (3-step first-run wizard).

* Fix WorkspaceNav.tsx APP_LINKS — the Projects tab pointed at /dashboard
  and the Accounts tab pointed at /accounts (no such route). Now points at
  /projects and /connect respectively.

* Fix ProjectsPage.tsx — was passing active="/dashboard" to WorkspaceNav
  instead of active="/projects".

Verification:
* `bun run typecheck` — clean
* `bun test` — 40/40 pass
* `bun run build` — succeeds (433 KB JS, 78 KB CSS)
* Dev server probes: all 8 new page routes return 200; all 12 API proxy
  wildcards reach the proxy (503 because no backend running, NOT 404).
